WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.450
Alveolar injury changes both
the barrier and the airspace.

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:07.237
In the exudative phase
of acute respiratory distress syndrome,

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:11.438
damage increases permeability of
the alveolar and capillary membrane.

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:16.191
Fluid crosses into the
lung, and surfactant becomes inactivated.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:18.931
Watch the airspace shrink as fluid accumulates.

00:00:19.560 --> 00:00:21.700
Oxygen exchange is now impaired by more than a

00:00:21.740 --> 00:00:22.953
shortage of inspired air.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:26.057
The next view shows repair and proliferation.

00:00:26.610 --> 00:00:30.700
The supplied chapter describes
type two pneumocytes, fibroblasts, and

00:00:30.700 --> 00:00:32.528
myofibroblasts during this phase.

00:00:32.860 --> 00:00:36.543
In a fibrotic phase,
remodeling and alveolar destruction further

00:00:36.560 --> 00:00:38.009
disrupt the exchange surface.

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:42.613
These are source-described stages,
with overlapping time ranges, not

00:00:42.660 --> 00:00:44.523
an inevitable clock for every patient.

00:00:44.940 --> 00:00:48.394
Keep this process separate
from bronchial asthma: asthma narrows

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:52.340
the conducting airway through
smooth muscle contraction, swelling, and

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:52.692
mucus.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:57.123
ARDS damages the alveolar
and capillary exchange region.
